-- A `case` inside a block has its branches right of the block's column
-- (language.md §12.2, B5): §4's "branches may sit at the `case` keyword's
-- own column" does not reach a `case` that begins an item, because a
-- pattern at the block's column begins the next item. The `case` has no
-- branches, case_without_branches at 10:5 — an error, never another program.
-- The rest of the line reads as the next item, `Just n`, and its `->` as
-- a token no item continues with, and each is reported as what it then is.
f : Maybe Int → Int
f x =
    case x of
    Just n → n
    Nothing → 0
